1
00:00:43,859 --> 00:00:45,820
Yu Gyeom and I...

2
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:48,688
haven't changed at all.

3
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,228
But...

4
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,489
Sae Ryeong and Yu Gyeom...

5
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:04,836
have clearly changed.

6
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:37,864
[6. Fate]

7
00:01:52,753 --> 00:01:53,880
Ha Yeon.

8
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,322
[Episode 6]

9
00:02:31,295 --> 00:02:32,551
Mom!

10
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:35,127
Take this out?

11
00:02:35,127 --> 00:02:37,093
No, hold on a second.

12
00:03:01,366 --> 00:03:03,505
Are you free this afternoon?

13
00:03:03,505 --> 00:03:05,102
Yes.

14
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:06,353
That smells good.

15
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:07,688
- Nice, isn't it?
- Yeah.

16
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:09,722
Smell this. I just bought it.

17
00:03:09,722 --> 00:03:11,773
It smells so good.

18
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,706
Damn. Hey!

19
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:42,826
Seriously.

20
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:03,509
Oh no! My milk!

21
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:15,565
"Oh no! My milk!"

22
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:23,215
Damn it!

23
00:04:35,398 --> 00:04:36,694
Ha Yeon,

24
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,060
did you get a phone?

25
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,120
I see.

26
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,577
Oh my!

27
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:48,293
Sorry! What do I do?

28
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,350
Jin Mi, Jin Mi, Jin Mi.

29
00:04:56,350 --> 00:04:58,703
Can we come over to your place today?

30
00:04:59,426 --> 00:05:01,100
Is my house really okay?

31
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:04,096
It's not a three-story mansion.

32
00:05:04,096 --> 00:05:07,140
What does that matter?

33
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,350
True.

34
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:10,602
But at least my house is actually mine.

35
00:05:10,602 --> 00:05:13,723
Not a fake house you clean for someone else?

36
00:05:22,364 --> 00:05:24,491
Move over!

37
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:31,343
Hey, Lee Won Bae!

38
00:05:31,343 --> 00:05:33,580
- Hello?
- Where's Kim Ha Yeon?

39
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:35,393
Kim Ha Yeon?

40
00:05:35,393 --> 00:05:36,615
She's not here.

41
00:05:41,341 --> 00:05:43,042
Kim Ha Yeon sits here, right?

42
00:05:43,042 --> 00:05:44,860
Yeah! It is!

43
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:45,909
Hey.

44
00:05:52,947 --> 00:05:54,289
Hey.

45
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:58,018
Why are you reading? That's not like you.

46
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,054
Hey.

47
00:06:02,054 --> 00:06:03,427
Can't you hear me?

48
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:10,435
- Hey, your hair's got--
- Seriously.

49
00:06:12,035 --> 00:06:13,245
What is it?

50
00:06:13,916 --> 00:06:15,105
Is it gum?

51
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:19,463
Hey.

52
00:06:23,312 --> 00:06:24,558
Hey.

53
00:06:24,558 --> 00:06:26,036
Yeah, I'm out too.

54
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,506
Hey. Sung Sae Ryeong.

55
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:41,722
Are you being bullied?

56
00:06:46,024 --> 00:06:48,309
Well, she is being bullied.

57
00:06:48,309 --> 00:06:52,803
Even Lee Won Bae totally ignores her.
His girlfriend's the ringleader.

58
00:06:52,803 --> 00:06:55,638
Sung Sae Ryeong wasted her whole damn life.

59
00:06:55,638 --> 00:06:57,434
Nobody's on her side.

60
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:03,537
But your girlfriend doesn't give a damn.
She's totally doing her own thing.

61
00:07:04,411 --> 00:07:06,055
She just minds her own business.

62
00:07:06,055 --> 00:07:08,378
Doesn't even seem interested.

63
00:07:08,378 --> 00:07:12,905
Honestly, I don't know if she's pretty,
but she seems the most normal.

64
00:07:17,532 --> 00:07:19,291
I think she's pretty.

65
00:07:21,391 --> 00:07:22,813
Are you nuts?

66
00:07:48,118 --> 00:07:50,137
Excuse me.

67
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:51,598
Yes?

68
00:07:51,598 --> 00:07:53,415
This is my seat.

69
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:56,547
Okay.

70
00:07:59,798 --> 00:08:03,358
And were you looking at me?

71
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:04,391
What?

72
00:08:04,391 --> 00:08:06,331
Please stop staring at me.

73
00:08:06,331 --> 00:08:08,091
I might get the wrong idea.

74
00:08:10,925 --> 00:08:12,343
No, that's... what...

75
00:08:12,343 --> 00:08:15,612
I'll be in the restroom.
Please be out of my seat by then.

76
00:08:15,612 --> 00:08:16,778
Well, then.

77
00:08:45,392 --> 00:08:46,710
Excuse me.

78
00:08:48,487 --> 00:08:50,605
This is my seat.

79
00:08:50,605 --> 00:08:52,565
Get lost.

80
00:08:52,565 --> 00:08:56,012
And were you looking at me?

81
00:08:56,012 --> 00:08:57,263
Jung Yeon.

82
00:08:58,830 --> 00:08:59,911
Get lost.

83
00:08:59,911 --> 00:09:01,816
Please stop staring at me.

84
00:09:01,816 --> 00:09:03,472
I might get the wrong idea.

85
00:09:03,472 --> 00:09:06,237
Damn it! Get lost!

86
00:09:06,237 --> 00:09:08,970
- Kim Jung Yeon.
- I said, get lost!

87
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:22,704
I really don't know where to turn.

88
00:09:22,704 --> 00:09:25,601
I wasn't talking to you, Mom...

89
00:09:26,942 --> 00:09:32,469
Ha Yeon is so hard to deal with, you know?

90
00:09:34,171 --> 00:09:38,516
But you've never given me a hard time.

91
00:09:38,516 --> 00:09:40,691
You know that, right, Jung Yeon?

92
00:09:40,691 --> 00:09:43,032
Yes. I know.

93
00:09:43,032 --> 00:09:47,246
Could you talk to Ha Yeon for me?

94
00:09:47,246 --> 00:09:48,864
About what?

95
00:09:50,552 --> 00:09:52,390
Tell her to study. Please. No, no.

96
00:09:52,390 --> 00:09:55,095
Forget studying. Just tell her to listen to me.

97
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:56,967
If only she were like you. Okay?

98
00:09:56,967 --> 00:10:00,512
Jung Yeon, you really don't have any problems.

99
00:10:06,212 --> 00:10:07,565
Why?

100
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:11,273
So you think it's a joke too?

101
00:10:12,905 --> 00:10:14,211
No.

102
00:10:14,885 --> 00:10:17,192
I'll try talking to her.

103
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:20,125
Where are you going?

104
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:24,114
Just out front.

105
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:26,221
Okay, Jung Yeon.

106
00:10:26,221 --> 00:10:29,616
You're the only one I trust.

107
00:10:57,950 --> 00:11:00,225
That's my seat.

108
00:11:00,225 --> 00:11:02,733
You don't have to get up...

109
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:07,357
It's just that when I come here,
I always sit in this seat.

110
00:11:07,357 --> 00:11:09,866
Sit down. Please, sit.

111
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:23,368
Okay. Did that upset you?

112
00:11:24,425 --> 00:11:25,660
No.

113
00:11:27,745 --> 00:11:29,968
We're using sign language, right?

114
00:11:31,657 --> 00:11:34,083
What would you like to drink?

115
00:11:34,736 --> 00:11:37,219
I'll have an iced Americano.

116
00:11:37,219 --> 00:11:41,285
I'll have cinnamon...

117
00:11:41,285 --> 00:11:42,734
Something with cinnamon.

118
00:11:42,734 --> 00:11:44,339
No whipped cream.

119
00:11:45,332 --> 00:11:46,846
Cinnamon Frappuccino.

120
00:11:46,846 --> 00:11:49,286
Cinnamon Frappuccino!

121
00:11:54,882 --> 00:11:56,263
Excuse me.

122
00:11:57,338 --> 00:11:59,451
Do you have any relatives in Seoul?

123
00:12:00,070 --> 00:12:01,096
Sorry?

124
00:12:01,096 --> 00:12:02,554
Relatives.

125
00:12:02,554 --> 00:12:06,435
To be good at signing, you need
someone who can't hear or speak.

126
00:12:06,435 --> 00:12:08,512
My second-oldest sister lives in Seoul.

127
00:12:08,512 --> 00:12:10,689
She can't speak or hear.

128
00:12:10,689 --> 00:12:12,052
Did she die?

129
00:12:13,471 --> 00:12:14,854
No.

130
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:21,943
But Jung Yeon, don't you know it's
rude to ask about that kind of thing?

131
00:12:24,953 --> 00:12:26,867
I'm sorry.

132
00:12:26,867 --> 00:12:28,388
It's okay.

133
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:34,000
You know what?

134
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,500
There are no college students in this town.

135
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:40,292
So when I meet a college student,

136
00:12:40,292 --> 00:12:42,584
I find it a little fascinating.

137
00:12:42,584 --> 00:12:47,876
But out of all the college students,

138
00:12:47,876 --> 00:12:50,918
you seem the most fascinating.

139
00:12:54,348 --> 00:12:55,988
That was hard?

140
00:12:55,988 --> 00:13:01,030
That was... you know what?

141
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:06,595
"There are no college students in this town."

142
00:13:06,595 --> 00:13:13,710
"So I find college students a bit fascinating."

143
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:15,188
But--

144
00:13:18,465 --> 00:13:20,091
Hey, what about tomorrow?

145
00:13:20,091 --> 00:13:21,321
Aren't you coming?

146
00:13:21,321 --> 00:13:22,969
Everyone's waiting for you.

147
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:25,212
Kim Jung Yeon, have you been studying lately?

148
00:13:25,212 --> 00:13:26,515
Lost the top spot?

149
00:13:26,515 --> 00:13:27,959
I said no...

150
00:13:29,414 --> 00:13:31,381
I'll go. What time tomorrow?

151
00:13:33,081 --> 00:13:35,486
You said students fascinate you.

152
00:13:35,486 --> 00:13:36,576
Sorry?

153
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:43,178
It's because everyone here
goes to Seoul after high school.

154
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:47,247
Want to see lots of students tomorrow?

155
00:13:48,087 --> 00:13:49,872
Let's go to Seoul together.

156
00:13:49,872 --> 00:13:51,540
What do you think?

157
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:52,749
What?

158
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:56,232
You said a cinnamon Frappuccino,
no whipped cream.

159
00:13:56,232 --> 00:13:58,776
U-Um...

160
00:14:00,841 --> 00:14:02,269
whipped cream...

161
00:14:03,177 --> 00:14:04,930
That's the whole reason I drink it.

162
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:06,351
Um...

163
00:14:08,174 --> 00:14:09,654
Seung Chan.

164
00:14:09,654 --> 00:14:12,608
I had a bicycle, you know?

165
00:14:12,608 --> 00:14:13,663
So?

166
00:14:14,855 --> 00:14:18,140
"I'm borrowing it for a bit."

167
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:19,443
Who could it be?

168
00:14:19,443 --> 00:14:25,368
Who the hell around you writes handwritten
notes in this age of phones?

169
00:14:25,368 --> 00:14:26,445
Hurry up.

170
00:14:27,618 --> 00:14:30,213
Damn. I'm so hot.

171
00:14:33,028 --> 00:14:35,904
Oh my. What the hell? Why's she staring? Jerk.

172
00:14:40,064 --> 00:14:42,101
Damn!

173
00:14:42,101 --> 00:14:44,941
Damn it! Damn it!

174
00:15:04,209 --> 00:15:05,304
Here.

175
00:15:05,304 --> 00:15:06,714
Thanks.

176
00:15:08,928 --> 00:15:10,557
You drink well.

177
00:15:14,761 --> 00:15:16,166
What's this, though?

178
00:15:16,166 --> 00:15:18,189
This? A bicycle.

179
00:15:18,861 --> 00:15:22,701
I mean, how did you get this?

180
00:15:22,701 --> 00:15:25,214
Do you know how to ride?

181
00:15:25,214 --> 00:15:26,262
Yeah.

182
00:15:29,325 --> 00:15:30,391
What?

183
00:15:30,391 --> 00:15:31,792
- One.
- Wait.

184
00:15:31,792 --> 00:15:32,918
- Two.
- Wait!

185
00:15:32,918 --> 00:15:35,272
- Three.
- Wait.

186
00:15:35,272 --> 00:15:37,437
Come with me!

187
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:40,107
- I'll wait for you.
- Why so slow?

188
00:15:40,107 --> 00:15:42,143
Hey, are you okay?

189
00:15:48,768 --> 00:15:50,160
We're here.

190
00:15:51,015 --> 00:15:52,601
Where is this?

191
00:15:52,601 --> 00:15:54,454
Here?

192
00:15:54,454 --> 00:15:56,307
Firefly Hill.

193
00:15:56,988 --> 00:15:58,658
Fireflies?

194
00:15:58,658 --> 00:15:59,888
Yeah.

195
00:15:59,888 --> 00:16:02,315
There's a festival here every summer.

196
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:08,691
When it gets pitch dark,
this place fills with fireflies.

197
00:16:11,054 --> 00:16:13,674
It must be so pretty.

198
00:16:13,674 --> 00:16:14,819
Yeah.

199
00:16:14,819 --> 00:16:16,588
So I came to see it early.

200
00:16:17,352 --> 00:16:18,854
Why?

201
00:16:18,854 --> 00:16:20,645
You can just come that day.

202
00:16:21,254 --> 00:16:23,594
I can't see this then.

203
00:16:23,594 --> 00:16:25,296
Why can't you?

204
00:16:27,188 --> 00:16:32,832
Many guests come that day, so my grandfather
drags me around to greet everyone.

205
00:16:37,348 --> 00:16:39,055
I see.

206
00:17:00,368 --> 00:17:01,476
Let's go.

207
00:17:11,823 --> 00:17:13,194
I...

208
00:17:13,934 --> 00:17:15,850
haven't changed.

209
00:17:17,841 --> 00:17:19,902
I couldn't change.

210
00:17:28,601 --> 00:17:30,291
[5-minute caricatures, only 1,000 won]

211
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:31,608
[Upo-ri Firefly Festival]

212
00:17:34,958 --> 00:17:36,826
It's the festival!

213
00:17:39,685 --> 00:17:41,933
- Grab it! Over here!
- Seriously.

214
00:17:47,959 --> 00:17:49,108
This.

215
00:17:58,061 --> 00:18:00,041
Why do you have this?

216
00:18:00,041 --> 00:18:02,471
I borrowed it from your mom.

217
00:18:02,471 --> 00:18:03,857
Give it back.

218
00:18:05,161 --> 00:18:06,868
Are you miserable?

219
00:18:10,757 --> 00:18:13,062
You're being bullied.

220
00:18:13,062 --> 00:18:15,098
I'm asking if you're miserable now.

221
00:18:16,688 --> 00:18:18,821
Yeah. It's miserable.

222
00:18:18,821 --> 00:18:22,172
The kids you bullied probably
felt the same way.

223
00:18:22,172 --> 00:18:23,471
I know.

224
00:18:23,471 --> 00:18:25,397
That's why I'm being punished, right?

225
00:18:25,397 --> 00:18:26,899
No.

226
00:18:26,899 --> 00:18:29,177
That has nothing to do with it.

227
00:18:29,177 --> 00:18:30,961
What are you talking about?

228
00:18:30,961 --> 00:18:33,464
Me getting fucked over is their goal.

229
00:18:33,464 --> 00:18:36,733
How happy they must be
to see me suffer like this.

230
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,567
No.

231
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:43,438
That really doesn't matter.

232
00:18:46,484 --> 00:18:53,167
Your victims couldn't care less
whether you fall apart or get punished.

233
00:18:54,171 --> 00:18:56,220
They only want one thing.

234
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:57,957
Tell me.

235
00:18:57,957 --> 00:19:00,992
What the hell do they want from me?

236
00:19:01,924 --> 00:19:04,910
A sincere apology from the perpetrator.

237
00:19:04,910 --> 00:19:09,195
So if you go to them and apologize,
saying you're so sorry, that you were wrong--

238
00:19:09,195 --> 00:19:12,400
Then you should sincerely
apologize to me first.

239
00:19:14,557 --> 00:19:16,364
- Me?
- Yeah.

240
00:19:16,364 --> 00:19:18,615
To me, you're the perpetrator.

241
00:19:20,202 --> 00:19:21,554
Hey.

242
00:19:21,554 --> 00:19:22,996
Why am I the perpetrator to you?

243
00:19:22,996 --> 00:19:25,037
- I'm like you--
- Kim Ha Yeon.

244
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:30,950
My life got messed up
exactly when you showed up.

245
00:19:32,258 --> 00:19:34,713
You stole my boyfriend.

246
00:19:34,713 --> 00:19:37,664
And that's why I'm being bullied now.

247
00:19:37,664 --> 00:19:38,807
Isn't it?

248
00:19:40,244 --> 00:19:44,475
And you're going to lecture me
about victims and perpetrators?

249
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:48,266
You've got some real nerve.

250
00:19:50,491 --> 00:19:52,035
That's because I...

251
00:19:54,023 --> 00:19:55,816
Because I've been bullied too.

252
00:19:55,816 --> 00:19:57,030
Right.

253
00:19:57,030 --> 00:20:00,096
And now you're the one bullying me.

254
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:04,726
What really wounds my pride

255
00:20:06,874 --> 00:20:09,982
is that I'm being put through this
by a nobody like you.

256
00:20:11,678 --> 00:20:12,759
But whatever.

257
00:20:12,759 --> 00:20:14,741
This will all end soon.

258
00:20:14,741 --> 00:20:16,371
I believe that.

259
00:20:18,818 --> 00:20:22,697
What are you counting on
to get out of being bullied?

260
00:20:24,884 --> 00:20:27,060
I'll take Cho Yu Gyeom back.

261
00:20:28,657 --> 00:20:30,538
From you. No matter what.

262
00:20:37,991 --> 00:20:40,398
Okay, everyone!

263
00:20:40,398 --> 00:20:43,493
Don't get too excited just
because we're finishing early today!

264
00:20:43,493 --> 00:20:45,121
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

265
00:21:32,793 --> 00:21:34,460
Damn. What's that?

266
00:21:51,176 --> 00:21:52,325
How do you like it?

267
00:21:52,325 --> 00:21:54,434
This is the world you gave me.

268
00:22:20,987 --> 00:22:23,296
You've never been to Seoul?

269
00:22:24,584 --> 00:22:27,181
No, I haven't.

270
00:22:27,181 --> 00:22:28,299
Why?

271
00:22:30,195 --> 00:22:32,961
I've had no reason to go.

272
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:41,951
But why do you want to understand
such fast signing, Jung Yeon?

273
00:22:41,951 --> 00:22:45,136
Honestly, understanding
this much is impressive.

274
00:22:49,591 --> 00:22:52,679
A person I know had parents
who used sign language.

275
00:22:52,679 --> 00:22:54,374
They signed so fast.

276
00:22:54,374 --> 00:22:56,411
Were they deaf, by any chance?

277
00:22:57,018 --> 00:22:58,060
Yes.

278
00:22:59,264 --> 00:23:01,642
I want to talk with them,

279
00:23:03,845 --> 00:23:09,240
but with what I know now,
I feel like I wouldn't understand anything.

280
00:23:10,298 --> 00:23:13,012
You said they're parents of someone you know.

281
00:23:13,012 --> 00:23:16,281
So is that person a friend?

282
00:23:46,078 --> 00:23:47,219
No.

283
00:23:49,054 --> 00:23:50,406
Just...

284
00:23:51,405 --> 00:23:52,820
someone I know.

285
00:23:58,313 --> 00:24:00,981
I wonder if the festival has started.

286
00:24:00,981 --> 00:24:04,191
Is it okay not to go there?

287
00:24:04,191 --> 00:24:06,433
I heard it's hosted by your family.

288
00:24:06,433 --> 00:24:08,448
I'm not needed.

289
00:24:08,448 --> 00:24:11,253
Our family only needs Yu Gyeom today.

290
00:24:15,372 --> 00:24:18,500
- Oh my, welcome.
- Oh my, oh my.

291
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:22,348
- Thank you for traveling so far.
- No, no.

292
00:24:23,130 --> 00:24:25,549
- And Yu Gyeom?
- Yes.

293
00:24:25,549 --> 00:24:29,320
He went in to change clothes.
He'll be out soon.

294
00:24:30,317 --> 00:24:31,448
Are you thirsty?

295
00:24:31,448 --> 00:24:32,973
No, I'm fine.

296
00:24:32,973 --> 00:24:35,318
- Hello there.
- Oh my.

297
00:24:35,318 --> 00:24:36,351
Yu Gyeom's mother!

298
00:24:36,351 --> 00:24:37,995
Yes, Father.

299
00:24:42,878 --> 00:24:44,262
Tell me!

300
00:24:44,262 --> 00:24:45,694
Where is Cho Dul Hee?

301
00:24:45,694 --> 00:24:48,318
Where's this family's second daughter?

302
00:24:48,318 --> 00:24:50,835
I told you, I don't know.

303
00:24:58,878 --> 00:25:00,834
[Smartphone repair shop]

304
00:25:00,834 --> 00:25:01,845
[HELLO]

305
00:25:04,963 --> 00:25:06,173
You must really be dead.

306
00:25:06,173 --> 00:25:09,611
But dead or not, I'll keep tormenting you.

307
00:25:09,611 --> 00:25:12,067
And you have no reason to feel wronged.

308
00:25:12,067 --> 00:25:14,551
Because you were maid material all along.

309
00:25:14,551 --> 00:25:17,226
Honestly, you're not the lead.

310
00:25:17,226 --> 00:25:18,823
Not anywhere.

311
00:25:20,224 --> 00:25:21,913
Does that make sense?

312
00:25:21,913 --> 00:25:25,485
How can this family be so calm
when no one knows where she is?

313
00:25:25,485 --> 00:25:27,430
That's so strange.

314
00:25:27,430 --> 00:25:28,542
It's not strange.

315
00:25:28,542 --> 00:25:30,138
Not strange at all.

316
00:25:30,138 --> 00:25:34,584
What's stranger is that you care about
that in this house. What are you talking about?

317
00:25:34,584 --> 00:25:37,558
And what do you care where Dul Hee is?

318
00:25:37,558 --> 00:25:39,809
Because she's mine.

319
00:25:39,809 --> 00:25:42,831
- What?
- Because everything here is mine.

320
00:25:42,831 --> 00:25:44,177
Come on.

321
00:25:44,795 --> 00:25:46,304
Hey, Jeong Hui Gyeong.

322
00:25:46,304 --> 00:25:48,598
What in this house is yours?

323
00:25:48,598 --> 00:25:50,179
No?

324
00:25:50,179 --> 00:25:52,111
It's all mine.

325
00:25:52,111 --> 00:25:55,827
Everything's mine, except your wife,
who calls me "Sister."

326
00:25:55,827 --> 00:25:59,032
So find out where that bitch Dul Hee is.

327
00:25:59,032 --> 00:26:02,557
How can you, her father,
have so little interest in her?

328
00:26:02,557 --> 00:26:05,399
Then again, you never cared about your wife.

329
00:26:05,399 --> 00:26:06,876
Stop it!

330
00:26:06,876 --> 00:26:08,262
Why?

331
00:26:08,262 --> 00:26:10,038
It's true.

332
00:26:10,038 --> 00:26:14,145
Otherwise, how could I come and go
in this house so freely?

333
00:26:14,145 --> 00:26:16,285
It's all because of you, Cho Jae Jin--

334
00:26:16,285 --> 00:26:18,858
Say Ji Yeong's name one more time.

335
00:26:19,478 --> 00:26:20,664
She...

336
00:26:20,664 --> 00:26:22,249
What?

337
00:26:23,378 --> 00:26:27,757
Now you're going to pretend
to be a decent husband?

338
00:26:27,757 --> 00:26:29,391
Look.

339
00:26:29,391 --> 00:26:32,962
You can show me your real self.

340
00:26:32,962 --> 00:26:37,501
Besides, you and I are equally dirty.

341
00:26:41,231 --> 00:26:43,796
Oh my, Yu Gyeom!

342
00:26:45,355 --> 00:26:47,815
My Yu Gyeom.

343
00:26:48,442 --> 00:26:51,015
Yu Gyeom, Yu Gyeom!

344
00:26:51,015 --> 00:26:52,665
My Yu Gyeom.

345
00:26:52,665 --> 00:26:53,888
How have you been?

346
00:26:53,888 --> 00:26:55,887
It's been such a long time!

347
00:26:55,887 --> 00:26:58,372
My Yu Gyeom.

348
00:26:58,372 --> 00:27:01,549
It's been so long since Mom's seen you!

349
00:27:03,364 --> 00:27:04,722
A week.

350
00:27:04,722 --> 00:27:06,960
Oh my. Is that so?

351
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:10,069
If Mom can't see you for even one day.

352
00:27:10,069 --> 00:27:11,690
Aunt.

353
00:27:11,690 --> 00:27:12,951
Yes?

354
00:27:12,951 --> 00:27:15,690
What is it, Yu Gyeom?

355
00:27:15,690 --> 00:27:17,999
You're my aunt.

356
00:27:17,999 --> 00:27:20,067
Why do you keep saying Mom?

357
00:27:20,891 --> 00:27:25,324
No. I'm your mom. No.

358
00:27:25,324 --> 00:27:27,596
An aunt counts as a mom, too.

359
00:27:27,596 --> 00:27:30,121
What's with you today, Yu Gyeom?

360
00:27:30,121 --> 00:27:32,655
Did something upset you?

361
00:27:32,655 --> 00:27:34,446
Then Aunt will give pocket money--

362
00:27:34,446 --> 00:27:35,860
Yu Gyeom.

363
00:27:37,625 --> 00:27:38,804
Sister.

364
00:27:38,804 --> 00:27:40,010
Mom.

365
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,495
Grandfather...

366
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:44,541
Hello.

367
00:27:44,541 --> 00:27:46,471
Mom, let's go.

368
00:27:46,471 --> 00:27:47,700
Okay.

369
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:10,715
So bitter.

370
00:28:10,715 --> 00:28:12,763
Hey, is he coming?

371
00:28:12,763 --> 00:28:15,078
Is Kim Jung Yeon coming?

372
00:28:15,078 --> 00:28:17,154
No idea. He did ask what time, though.

373
00:28:17,154 --> 00:28:20,524
I heard he's in the countryside.
Can he even come?

374
00:28:20,524 --> 00:28:22,391
Really?

375
00:28:22,391 --> 00:28:23,478
Why?

376
00:28:23,478 --> 00:28:25,137
His dad's a caddie.

377
00:28:25,137 --> 00:28:27,963
Apparently he's caddying for some golf pro.

378
00:28:27,963 --> 00:28:29,303
Damn.

379
00:28:29,303 --> 00:28:31,518
Is that why he ignored my texts?

380
00:28:31,518 --> 00:28:34,822
Really? He doesn't ignore my texts.

381
00:28:36,842 --> 00:28:38,489
Hey. Kim Jung Yeon's here!

382
00:28:44,141 --> 00:28:46,028
- Man.
- What?

383
00:28:46,028 --> 00:28:48,365
He brought a girlfriend.

384
00:28:49,646 --> 00:28:50,930
What's this?

385
00:28:50,930 --> 00:28:53,275
Did you stop seeing us because of a girlfriend?

386
00:28:53,275 --> 00:28:54,792
Not my girlfriend.

387
00:28:54,792 --> 00:28:57,691
Then what is she?

388
00:28:59,257 --> 00:29:01,866
Hello. I'm Hong Jin Hyeok.

389
00:29:01,866 --> 00:29:03,746
I'm Cho Sam Hee.

390
00:29:07,758 --> 00:29:09,908
You're still rude, Kim Hye Min.

391
00:29:13,345 --> 00:29:14,556
Drink up.

392
00:29:14,556 --> 00:29:16,207
They're paying.

393
00:29:18,311 --> 00:29:19,883
Come on, what is this?

394
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:21,763
Just friends?

395
00:29:21,763 --> 00:29:24,251
Is he really just your guy friend?

396
00:29:24,251 --> 00:29:26,302
Yes. Friends. That's right.

397
00:29:28,018 --> 00:29:29,485
Right. Jung Yeon.

398
00:29:29,485 --> 00:29:32,982
Can you tutor me in circuit theory?

399
00:29:34,158 --> 00:29:35,755
You're the top student.

400
00:29:35,755 --> 00:29:37,221
Hey, what?

401
00:29:37,221 --> 00:29:38,938
He lost the top spot.

402
00:29:38,938 --> 00:29:40,711
Ask Oh Ji Eun instead.

403
00:29:40,711 --> 00:29:44,038
- He lost the top spot?
- Yeah, this kid took first.

404
00:29:44,038 --> 00:29:45,281
This kid's the top?

405
00:29:45,281 --> 00:29:47,120
No, from the bottom.

406
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:49,122
- My hand.
- Stop messing around.

407
00:29:49,122 --> 00:29:51,312
- Cheers, cheers. Come on.
- What should I do?

408
00:29:53,961 --> 00:29:57,144
Honestly, you're not the lead.

409
00:29:57,144 --> 00:29:58,727
Not anywhere.

410
00:30:02,838 --> 00:30:07,561
What really wounds my pride...

411
00:30:09,324 --> 00:30:12,614
is that I'm being put through this
by a nobody like you.

412
00:30:14,257 --> 00:30:17,204
Because you were maid material.

413
00:30:18,402 --> 00:30:19,478
But whatever.

414
00:30:19,478 --> 00:30:21,373
This will all end soon.

415
00:30:21,373 --> 00:30:23,188
I believe that.

416
00:30:25,897 --> 00:30:28,188
I'll take Cho Yu Gyeom back.

417
00:30:28,964 --> 00:30:31,121
From you. No matter what.

418
00:30:40,167 --> 00:30:41,620
[Upo-ri Firefly Festival]

419
00:30:43,964 --> 00:30:46,388
- A water gun, please.
- Why that?

420
00:30:46,388 --> 00:30:49,080
One, two, three.

421
00:30:53,894 --> 00:30:56,981
- It's so pretty!
- I feel so good.

422
00:30:56,981 --> 00:30:58,985
- It's fun.
- So good.

423
00:31:00,527 --> 00:31:03,380
Your girlfriend bullies a friend
and is happy about it.

424
00:31:04,084 --> 00:31:06,206
- Hey, Shin Seung Chan!
- I said nothing.

425
00:31:06,206 --> 00:31:07,541
- What did you say?
- I said nothing.

426
00:31:07,541 --> 00:31:10,792
- Look what Sung Sae Ryeong did to us.
- I remember, I remember.

427
00:31:10,792 --> 00:31:13,522
- Her? She deserves it.
- No. Calm down.

428
00:31:14,938 --> 00:31:18,545
Then why didn't you act up
with her when she did?

429
00:31:18,545 --> 00:31:21,304
Why go crazy the second she broke up
with Cho Yu Gyeom?

430
00:31:21,304 --> 00:31:22,899
How cowardly.

431
00:31:22,899 --> 00:31:24,136
Cowardly?

432
00:31:24,136 --> 00:31:25,777
Yeah.

433
00:31:25,777 --> 00:31:29,188
I knew you were cunning,
but I never knew you were cowards.

434
00:31:30,684 --> 00:31:32,983
Nothing better to do than bully?

435
00:31:33,993 --> 00:31:35,114
I'm leaving.

436
00:31:35,114 --> 00:31:36,730
You guys have fun.

437
00:31:36,730 --> 00:31:38,649
- Yes! Bye, ma'am.
- No, no!

438
00:31:38,649 --> 00:31:42,688
She's mad again. Why'd you mess with her?

439
00:31:42,688 --> 00:31:44,210
Seriously.

440
00:31:45,809 --> 00:31:47,564
I only did it to have you.

441
00:31:48,275 --> 00:31:49,339
Sorry. I love you.

442
00:31:49,339 --> 00:31:51,078
Stop messing around.

443
00:31:51,078 --> 00:31:53,363
- Okay, okay.
- Hey, hey, hey.

444
00:31:53,363 --> 00:31:56,428
What should we eat? I'm damn hungry.

445
00:31:56,428 --> 00:31:59,091
Hey, why isn't Cho Yu Gyeom here yet?

446
00:31:59,091 --> 00:32:00,429
What are you doing?

447
00:32:00,429 --> 00:32:02,116
I'll show them

448
00:32:04,431 --> 00:32:06,583
that I'm not a coward.

449
00:32:16,520 --> 00:32:20,277
Sae Ryeong, will you come
to the firefly festival today?

450
00:32:26,809 --> 00:32:28,824
Who are you lying to?

451
00:32:28,824 --> 00:32:31,539
Sung Sae Ryeong, who shines everywhere.

452
00:32:31,539 --> 00:32:33,504
I miss you.

453
00:32:33,504 --> 00:32:36,915
I came with you every year.
It feels empty without you.

454
00:32:38,102 --> 00:32:40,793
Okay, I'm coming now.

455
00:32:40,793 --> 00:32:43,395
Oh my. Isn't that our Yu Gyeom?

456
00:32:43,395 --> 00:32:46,382
Yes, it's our Yu Gyeom.

457
00:32:46,382 --> 00:32:48,466
He's grown so much.

458
00:32:48,466 --> 00:32:51,167
Look how handsome he is.

459
00:32:51,167 --> 00:32:52,596
Who does he look like?

460
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:54,820
His father, of course.

461
00:32:56,424 --> 00:33:00,189
If you want to see this festival,
you need to go now.

462
00:33:00,189 --> 00:33:03,609
You'd need a spot on that hill to see it well.

463
00:33:03,609 --> 00:33:05,315
- Yes.
- Right.

464
00:33:05,315 --> 00:33:07,387
Yu Gyeom, good to see you.

465
00:33:07,387 --> 00:33:09,947
- See you again!
- Yes.

466
00:33:09,947 --> 00:33:11,262
Bye now.

467
00:33:11,262 --> 00:33:12,621
Come on, let's go.

468
00:33:13,557 --> 00:33:14,803
Grandfather.

469
00:33:15,579 --> 00:33:16,752
Yes?

470
00:33:16,752 --> 00:33:19,152
Can you keep Aunt from coming over?

471
00:33:23,677 --> 00:33:24,964
What did you say?

472
00:33:24,964 --> 00:33:28,000
Or if she comes, don't let her touch my hands.

473
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:30,316
Wiping them with alcohol wipes
every time is a pain.

474
00:33:30,316 --> 00:33:31,877
Cho Yu Gyeom.

475
00:33:35,557 --> 00:33:38,116
Yu Gyeom, there's someone outside...

476
00:33:39,247 --> 00:33:41,892
who's come looking for you.

477
00:33:42,918 --> 00:33:44,425
Who's looking for me, sir?

478
00:33:44,425 --> 00:33:48,288
I told her to come in,
but she keeps saying she'll wait outside.

479
00:33:48,288 --> 00:33:51,943
I asked who she was.
She said she was just a friend.

480
00:34:08,278 --> 00:34:09,520
Who are you?

481
00:34:13,530 --> 00:34:15,022
I said, who are you?

482
00:34:17,818 --> 00:34:19,860
Are you dating Kim Jung Yeon?

483
00:34:21,125 --> 00:34:22,721
We're not friends.

484
00:34:22,721 --> 00:34:24,650
Why are you talking down to me?

485
00:34:24,650 --> 00:34:26,672
Just answer the question.

486
00:34:30,744 --> 00:34:32,190
We're not dating.

487
00:34:33,958 --> 00:34:35,168
Right.

488
00:34:35,168 --> 00:34:37,327
Of course not.

489
00:34:37,327 --> 00:34:40,912
Then why the hell did he bring you along?

490
00:34:48,213 --> 00:34:49,765
But I will date him.

491
00:34:51,423 --> 00:34:52,478
What?

492
00:34:52,478 --> 00:34:57,366
I wasn't planning to, but you're so mean
that I suddenly want to date him.

493
00:34:59,014 --> 00:35:01,099
What are you saying?

494
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:03,188
You know how sometimes

495
00:35:03,188 --> 00:35:07,542
you think it was never yours to begin with
and don't even look at it,

496
00:35:07,542 --> 00:35:13,382
but someone keeps saying,
"No. You can't have it. Never."

497
00:35:13,382 --> 00:35:16,450
and it makes you want it even more.

498
00:35:16,450 --> 00:35:18,787
That's how I feel right now.

499
00:35:21,828 --> 00:35:23,218
Sure.

500
00:35:23,218 --> 00:35:24,883
Fine, try dating.

501
00:35:26,744 --> 00:35:30,057
As if Kim Jung Yeon would
date someone like you?

502
00:35:30,057 --> 00:35:33,592
Damn, you're such a hick.

503
00:35:33,592 --> 00:35:34,958
Hey.

504
00:35:34,958 --> 00:35:37,592
A hick nobody would take for free.

505
00:35:38,222 --> 00:35:40,905
Fine. Go ahead and date.

506
00:35:40,905 --> 00:35:43,055
Then I'll use formal speech with you.

507
00:35:44,124 --> 00:35:45,778
No.

508
00:35:45,778 --> 00:35:48,118
You don't have to.

509
00:35:48,118 --> 00:35:50,010
I'm younger anyway.

510
00:35:54,277 --> 00:35:55,313
Damn it!

511
00:35:55,313 --> 00:35:57,498
- What is it?
- What's wrong? Are you okay?

512
00:35:57,498 --> 00:35:59,843
- Are you okay?
- What happened?

513
00:36:05,862 --> 00:36:06,942
Where are you going?

514
00:36:06,942 --> 00:36:09,084
I should get going.

515
00:36:09,084 --> 00:36:10,319
Now?

516
00:36:10,319 --> 00:36:14,007
It's late, and since I'm in Seoul,
I have somewhere to stop by.

517
00:36:16,019 --> 00:36:17,167
Well then.

518
00:36:17,167 --> 00:36:18,981
Sam Hee, stay a little longer.

519
00:36:18,981 --> 00:36:20,180
We're just getting started.

520
00:36:20,180 --> 00:36:23,141
No, thank you. I had a great time today.

521
00:36:23,141 --> 00:36:24,599
I'll be going.

522
00:36:29,792 --> 00:36:31,243
Hey.

523
00:36:31,243 --> 00:36:32,388
What are you doing?

524
00:36:33,258 --> 00:36:36,000
You should take her home.

525
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,107
Come on, do I have to take her home?

526
00:36:38,107 --> 00:36:40,846
At least get her a taxi.

527
00:36:40,846 --> 00:36:42,069
Come on, quick.

528
00:36:43,064 --> 00:36:44,705
Go.

529
00:36:44,705 --> 00:36:46,368
I said, go already!

530
00:36:47,538 --> 00:36:49,298
He's handsome, but he has no sense.

531
00:36:50,698 --> 00:36:53,751
Jin Hyeok, you have the best sense.

532
00:36:58,552 --> 00:37:00,089
Where's he going?

533
00:37:01,763 --> 00:37:02,945
Drink.

534
00:37:04,177 --> 00:37:06,637
- Stop drinking.
- Drink.

535
00:37:11,481 --> 00:37:12,809
Why are you here?

536
00:37:16,396 --> 00:37:17,856
Why did you come?

537
00:37:22,784 --> 00:37:25,247
I want to see the fireflies.

538
00:37:28,297 --> 00:37:29,782
I can't go.

539
00:37:29,782 --> 00:37:31,363
Can't you go?

540
00:37:34,292 --> 00:37:36,882
I want you to go with me.

541
00:37:48,504 --> 00:37:49,863
Please.

542
00:38:07,798 --> 00:38:09,074
Excuse me.

543
00:38:11,864 --> 00:38:13,044
Excuse me!

544
00:38:15,471 --> 00:38:17,578
Why are you crying?

545
00:38:17,578 --> 00:38:19,531
What's wrong?

546
00:38:19,531 --> 00:38:20,971
No. Nothing.

547
00:38:21,924 --> 00:38:24,149
But w-why are you crying?

548
00:38:24,149 --> 00:38:25,457
It's just...

549
00:38:26,291 --> 00:38:28,560
that my pride is so hurt.

550
00:38:29,584 --> 00:38:34,504
I feel like a hick, like it's oozing out of me.

551
00:38:36,108 --> 00:38:37,804
It was Kim Hye Min.

552
00:38:38,861 --> 00:38:41,095
She talks so nastily.

553
00:38:41,095 --> 00:38:43,448
Forget it, okay?

554
00:38:43,448 --> 00:38:44,763
I'll apologize for her.

555
00:38:44,763 --> 00:38:45,868
I'm sorry.

556
00:38:45,868 --> 00:38:48,116
But it's not entirely wrong, either.

557
00:38:48,116 --> 00:38:51,417
That's not true. Who says that?

558
00:38:51,417 --> 00:38:54,251
I know I'm lacking... I know that.

559
00:38:56,433 --> 00:38:59,062
I know I'm lacking.

560
00:39:01,971 --> 00:39:03,145
I know.

561
00:39:03,969 --> 00:39:05,679
Even so.

562
00:39:05,679 --> 00:39:07,474
What can I do? I like you.

563
00:39:13,103 --> 00:39:14,558
Even so.

564
00:39:15,898 --> 00:39:17,793
What can I do? I like you.

565
00:39:18,437 --> 00:39:19,529
Yes?

566
00:39:21,490 --> 00:39:22,674
No.

567
00:39:23,644 --> 00:39:26,243
Just stop crying first.

568
00:39:26,243 --> 00:39:27,804
I like you.

569
00:39:27,804 --> 00:39:29,908
This is how I am.

570
00:39:29,908 --> 00:39:34,711
You talked to me first and asked to be friends.

571
00:39:34,711 --> 00:39:38,471
I know that wasn't because you liked me.

572
00:39:38,471 --> 00:39:45,435
But I'm someone who
gives my heart away too easily.

573
00:39:45,435 --> 00:39:49,084
Then I just suddenly
like everything about them.

574
00:39:49,084 --> 00:39:53,547
I just fall hopelessly. That's just how I am.

575
00:39:54,139 --> 00:39:59,667
So that nasty woman told me to go ahead
and date you if I could.

576
00:39:59,667 --> 00:40:02,528
So I got really angry.

577
00:40:02,528 --> 00:40:06,251
Wait, what are you even talking about?

578
00:40:06,251 --> 00:40:07,706
Anyway,

579
00:40:09,791 --> 00:40:11,997
I like you, so please answer.

580
00:40:14,938 --> 00:40:19,228
But we, we haven't known each other very long.

581
00:40:19,228 --> 00:40:21,588
I know.

582
00:40:21,588 --> 00:40:24,647
But I felt this way from the start.

583
00:40:26,785 --> 00:40:28,053
But.

584
00:40:28,053 --> 00:40:29,599
As for me,

585
00:40:30,404 --> 00:40:32,726
I'm impatient. I can't wait long.

586
00:40:33,398 --> 00:40:35,946
Please answer by tomorrow.

587
00:40:35,946 --> 00:40:38,144
It's fine if it's a no.

588
00:40:39,044 --> 00:40:42,799
I know you'll say no anyway.

589
00:40:43,538 --> 00:40:45,307
But you really have to

590
00:40:46,071 --> 00:40:47,666
give me an answer.

591
00:40:48,611 --> 00:40:50,287
That way, I think I'll...

592
00:40:51,657 --> 00:40:54,024
be able to give up.

593
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:05,257
Hey.

594
00:41:05,257 --> 00:41:07,892
Why did we call Sung Sae Ryeong anyway?

595
00:41:08,511 --> 00:41:11,231
Hey, they said we're cowards.

596
00:41:11,231 --> 00:41:13,385
We have to prove we're not.

597
00:41:14,516 --> 00:41:16,151
What do you mean?

598
00:41:18,659 --> 00:41:21,398
Hey, isn't that Sung Sae Ryeong?

599
00:41:38,749 --> 00:41:41,616
Hey, Sung Sae Ryeong is pretty, though.

600
00:41:45,364 --> 00:41:47,147
Hey, she's damn pretty.

601
00:42:00,878 --> 00:42:02,115
What?

602
00:42:02,115 --> 00:42:04,069
Did they make up? Damn.

603
00:42:04,069 --> 00:42:07,083
What? Seung Chan, you overreacted.

604
00:42:07,083 --> 00:42:08,251
What's this?

605
00:42:08,251 --> 00:42:09,429
Hey, you.

606
00:42:09,429 --> 00:42:11,792
Never mind. Hold your palm out.

607
00:42:11,792 --> 00:42:14,471
Are you apologizing to our Jin Mi or not?

608
00:42:14,471 --> 00:42:16,117
Apologize for what?

609
00:42:16,117 --> 00:42:19,258
You should apologize. You snapped first.

610
00:42:19,258 --> 00:42:21,882
As a decent person, I think
he should apologize.

611
00:42:21,882 --> 00:42:22,987
Of course he should.

612
00:42:22,987 --> 00:42:24,589
But Kim Jin Mi.

613
00:42:24,589 --> 00:42:27,006
Damn it. Why are you linking arms with me?

614
00:42:27,006 --> 00:42:28,507
What's wrong?

615
00:42:28,507 --> 00:42:30,884
I said I wanted to see you, Sung Sae Ryeong.

616
00:42:30,884 --> 00:42:33,369
Knock it off, you crazy bitch. I know you.

617
00:42:33,369 --> 00:42:35,554
Shut up, Sung Sae Ryeong.

618
00:42:35,554 --> 00:42:37,957
I've still got so much to do to you.

619
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:41,562
So that's why you wanted to see me, bitch?

620
00:42:41,562 --> 00:42:43,054
Of course.

621
00:42:43,054 --> 00:42:45,885
I have to humiliate you completely.

622
00:42:45,885 --> 00:42:48,137
I have to drag you to hell.

623
00:42:48,137 --> 00:42:49,975
Only then can I sleep in peace.

624
00:42:49,975 --> 00:42:51,054
Oh my!

625
00:42:51,054 --> 00:42:54,052
Why should I go to hell so you can sleep well?

626
00:42:54,052 --> 00:42:56,209
Oh my! Sung Sae Ryeong.

627
00:42:56,209 --> 00:42:59,083
For everything you did to the kids at school,

628
00:42:59,083 --> 00:43:03,294
I'm going to pay you back,
because I'm not a coward.

629
00:43:04,246 --> 00:43:05,471
What the hell are you saying?

630
00:43:05,471 --> 00:43:07,644
Smile, you bitch.

631
00:43:20,392 --> 00:43:23,343
This isn't Firefly Hill.

632
00:43:24,565 --> 00:43:25,683
No, it isn't.

633
00:43:27,692 --> 00:43:29,584
Why are we going this way?

634
00:43:31,298 --> 00:43:32,477
Give me your hand.

635
00:43:47,079 --> 00:43:49,275
The fireflies look better from here.

636
00:43:52,958 --> 00:43:54,335
Close your eyes.

637
00:44:05,858 --> 00:44:08,434
Slowly open your eyes and look up.

638
00:44:23,163 --> 00:44:25,134
Can you see them?

639
00:44:25,134 --> 00:44:26,485
Yeah.

640
00:44:26,485 --> 00:44:28,499
They're sparkling.

641
00:44:53,737 --> 00:44:55,310
Avoiding me again?

642
00:45:00,626 --> 00:45:04,110
Can you tell me why you avoided me?

643
00:45:11,512 --> 00:45:12,775
Tell me.

644
00:45:20,596 --> 00:45:21,990
The thought of you...

645
00:45:25,592 --> 00:45:28,891
with Sae Ryeong kept coming back.

646
00:45:31,465 --> 00:45:34,335
The image of you holding Sae Ryeong

647
00:45:35,146 --> 00:45:38,029
wouldn't leave my head.

648
00:45:39,698 --> 00:45:43,121
You know very well why I did that.

649
00:45:45,412 --> 00:45:47,049
Yeah,

650
00:45:47,049 --> 00:45:48,313
I know.

651
00:45:49,291 --> 00:45:50,927
I know, but...

652
00:45:53,125 --> 00:45:58,026
you and Sae Ryeong are always
the main characters, and I feel like I'm not.

653
00:45:58,026 --> 00:46:01,246
And you were too good for me from the start.

654
00:46:01,246 --> 00:46:04,010
And we have nothing in common.

655
00:46:05,390 --> 00:46:09,996
And Sae Ryeong says I'm
actually the one who wronged her.

656
00:46:11,579 --> 00:46:14,387
So all those things keep getting to me.

657
00:46:14,387 --> 00:46:15,823
Over and over.

658
00:46:31,159 --> 00:46:33,611
But I'm going to change now.

659
00:46:34,399 --> 00:46:35,843
How?

660
00:46:39,979 --> 00:46:42,607
Into someone who suits you.

661
00:46:43,632 --> 00:46:47,714
A confident, self-assured person.

662
00:46:51,812 --> 00:46:53,181
Like this.

663
00:47:27,890 --> 00:47:29,047
Excuse me.

664
00:47:30,601 --> 00:47:32,283
Are you all right?

665
00:47:49,575 --> 00:47:53,345
It's so pretty.

666
00:47:53,345 --> 00:47:55,636
- Want to sit there? Yeah.
- There?

667
00:47:59,460 --> 00:48:01,644
Amazing.

668
00:48:02,299 --> 00:48:04,726
What's that? It's cute.

669
00:48:04,726 --> 00:48:06,264
- Cute, right?
- Yes.

670
00:48:10,893 --> 00:48:12,193
Hold on.

671
00:48:22,299 --> 00:48:23,606
What are you doing?

672
00:48:24,313 --> 00:48:25,700
I'm going to listen to music.

673
00:48:30,452 --> 00:48:31,671
What's this?

674
00:48:31,671 --> 00:48:32,703
This?

675
00:48:33,492 --> 00:48:34,988
A cassette tape.

676
00:48:36,565 --> 00:48:39,336
Is it like an LP?

677
00:48:39,336 --> 00:48:41,581
It's newer than that.

678
00:48:41,581 --> 00:48:43,072
Then a CD?

679
00:48:43,072 --> 00:48:44,694
Older than that.

680
00:48:53,202 --> 00:48:54,502
What's this song?

681
00:48:54,502 --> 00:48:55,712
This song?

682
00:48:57,643 --> 00:49:01,556
Kona's "A Witch Sets Off on a Journey."

683
00:49:04,986 --> 00:49:06,734
I've never heard it.

684
00:49:09,341 --> 00:49:10,663
Me neither.

685
00:49:12,756 --> 00:49:15,393
When I hear this song, I'll think of you.

686
00:49:19,195 --> 00:49:20,503
Yu Gyeom.

687
00:49:21,837 --> 00:49:23,801
What do you want to be?

688
00:49:25,283 --> 00:49:26,470
Me?

689
00:49:31,302 --> 00:49:32,643
As for me,

690
00:49:34,190 --> 00:49:36,097
I just want to leave my house.

691
00:49:37,076 --> 00:49:38,249
What about you?

692
00:49:47,368 --> 00:49:49,010
I...

693
00:49:54,102 --> 00:49:56,299
I want to be something.

694
00:49:58,144 --> 00:49:59,455
Please.

695
00:50:08,550 --> 00:50:12,316
How much vacation is left?

696
00:50:38,956 --> 00:50:42,360
Damn. In two weeks the sweet life is over.

697
00:50:43,929 --> 00:50:49,719
Damn. We're not seniors yet, but they'll
treat us like seniors and ride us hard.

698
00:50:49,719 --> 00:50:52,186
I haven't done anything.

699
00:50:52,186 --> 00:50:53,950
What if I don't get into college?

700
00:50:53,950 --> 00:50:55,455
Yeah, you probably won't.

701
00:50:55,455 --> 00:50:57,892
- Yeah, you too.
- You too.

702
00:50:58,970 --> 00:51:00,630
What are they doing?

703
00:51:02,290 --> 00:51:03,387
What else?

704
00:51:03,387 --> 00:51:06,497
Kim Jin Mi is ostracizing Sung Sae Ryeong.

705
00:51:06,497 --> 00:51:08,977
Please. Making up, my ass.

706
00:51:08,977 --> 00:51:10,897
I didn't buy it from the start.

707
00:51:11,670 --> 00:51:12,804
No.

708
00:51:12,804 --> 00:51:15,409
They definitely made up earlier.

709
00:51:15,409 --> 00:51:17,995
We saw it. Right?

710
00:51:17,995 --> 00:51:20,030
Hey, Lee Won Bae.

711
00:51:20,030 --> 00:51:21,727
You call that making up?

712
00:51:24,310 --> 00:51:26,948
- Hey, what's this?
- Come on.

713
00:51:28,904 --> 00:51:30,262
Have you lost it?

714
00:51:30,262 --> 00:51:31,884
Hey. I told you.

715
00:51:31,884 --> 00:51:33,969
I'm all about fucking justice.

716
00:51:33,969 --> 00:51:36,894
You crazy bitch, you hurt us all.
I'm getting revenge for them!

717
00:51:36,894 --> 00:51:37,928
Why?

718
00:51:37,928 --> 00:51:39,500
Because everyone wants it!

719
00:51:39,500 --> 00:51:43,103
So I bravely stepped up for everyone
and am tormenting you like this!

720
00:51:43,103 --> 00:51:44,947
Just like you did to me.

721
00:51:44,947 --> 00:51:45,972
Got it?

722
00:51:46,970 --> 00:51:48,054
Yeah?

723
00:51:48,054 --> 00:51:50,076
But I never hit you.

724
00:51:50,076 --> 00:51:51,403
Or shoved you like this?

725
00:51:51,403 --> 00:51:53,930
Fuck. You did everything but that!

726
00:51:53,930 --> 00:51:56,357
Seriously. Justice? Brave?

727
00:51:56,357 --> 00:51:58,030
What? What else?

728
00:51:59,199 --> 00:52:01,414
Not a coward?

729
00:52:01,414 --> 00:52:04,285
Hey. You're a complete idiot.

730
00:52:04,285 --> 00:52:07,958
You look like an idiot,
and your actions and thoughts are all idiotic.

731
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:10,262
Why on earth were you born like that?

732
00:52:10,964 --> 00:52:14,125
Well, some people are like that
from the day they're born.

733
00:52:14,125 --> 00:52:16,759
- Everything about you stinks!
- What?

734
00:52:16,759 --> 00:52:17,801
- Hey.
- What?

735
00:52:17,801 --> 00:52:20,502
Hey! Kim Jin Mi! You really shouldn't do this.

736
00:52:20,502 --> 00:52:24,641
Revenge for everyone, my ass!
Who says you get to take revenge?

737
00:52:24,641 --> 00:52:25,721
Because I'm the queen!

738
00:52:25,721 --> 00:52:27,186
I'm the queen now!

739
00:52:27,186 --> 00:52:30,467
Excuse me. Can anyone be a queen?

740
00:52:30,467 --> 00:52:33,362
You're a servant for life. Born that way.

741
00:52:33,362 --> 00:52:35,948
Damn. Go look in a mirror sometime.

742
00:52:35,948 --> 00:52:38,442
A queen who looks like you?
I've never seen one.

743
00:52:38,442 --> 00:52:39,638
What did you say?

744
00:52:39,638 --> 00:52:40,869
- Hey.
- What?

745
00:52:40,869 --> 00:52:42,746
Hey, wait. Hey, Jin Mi.

746
00:52:42,746 --> 00:52:44,012
Hey, this is bad.

747
00:52:44,012 --> 00:52:46,074
What do we do?

748
00:52:46,074 --> 00:52:49,416
This is too much. Shouldn't we report it?

749
00:52:49,416 --> 00:52:51,454
Please, just grow up already.

750
00:52:51,454 --> 00:52:53,670
Hey, Shin Seung Chan! Listen up.

751
00:52:53,670 --> 00:52:57,909
I'm not a coward.
Would a coward do this to her?

752
00:52:57,909 --> 00:53:00,389
- I'm going to wreck this bitch today.
- Damn.

753
00:53:00,389 --> 00:53:02,432
Is she talking to me?

754
00:53:02,432 --> 00:53:04,612
Yeah, I think so.

755
00:53:04,612 --> 00:53:08,105
Was I the only one bullying?
Kim Jin Mi, you're an accomplice!

756
00:53:08,105 --> 00:53:10,816
Acting all clean and righteous! Cut the crap!

757
00:53:10,816 --> 00:53:12,156
Seriously.

758
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:20,656
Damn.

759
00:53:20,656 --> 00:53:22,213
You came just in time.

760
00:53:22,213 --> 00:53:24,387
Stop them. What's wrong with them?

761
00:53:24,387 --> 00:53:26,373
- How did you get here?
- She'll go bald.

762
00:53:26,373 --> 00:53:29,332
- Let go!
- You let go! Damn.

763
00:53:32,004 --> 00:53:33,566
Damn!

764
00:53:48,809 --> 00:53:50,262
Crazy bitch.

765
00:53:50,262 --> 00:53:52,024
What good is looking polished?

766
00:53:52,024 --> 00:53:54,151
Damn. Wearing a holey undershirt!

767
00:53:54,151 --> 00:53:56,936
Hey! If you have time, look in a mirror too.

768
00:53:56,936 --> 00:53:59,335
Wearing that crappy underwear!

769
00:54:06,863 --> 00:54:08,616
Damn, wait for me.

770
00:54:17,385 --> 00:54:18,804
Hey.

771
00:54:18,804 --> 00:54:20,357
Give it a rest.

772
00:54:23,847 --> 00:54:25,206
Where are you going?

773
00:54:25,811 --> 00:54:27,768
Don't go anywhere! I'm not done!

774
00:54:27,768 --> 00:54:29,551
- It's over.
- It's not over!

775
00:54:29,551 --> 00:54:31,484
Stop it, Jin Mi!

776
00:54:35,733 --> 00:54:37,334
Kim Jin Mi.

777
00:54:40,822 --> 00:54:43,507
Straighten your back. What is that?

778
00:55:28,290 --> 00:55:30,539
[Upo High School]

779
00:55:30,539 --> 00:55:31,971
I heard they got in a huge fight.

780
00:55:31,971 --> 00:55:34,329
I should've seen that.

781
00:55:41,992 --> 00:55:43,327
Ha Yeon.

782
00:55:53,180 --> 00:55:54,258
Here.

783
00:55:57,739 --> 00:55:59,133
What's this?

784
00:55:59,133 --> 00:56:00,202
I didn't buy it.

785
00:56:00,202 --> 00:56:02,226
My mom used it.

786
00:56:02,226 --> 00:56:03,566
My mom said,

787
00:56:04,480 --> 00:56:06,554
give it to my girlfriend someday.

788
00:56:21,432 --> 00:56:23,247
Hey, what are you doing?

789
00:56:23,953 --> 00:56:25,179
I told you.

790
00:56:25,179 --> 00:56:26,631
I'm not done yet.

791
00:56:26,631 --> 00:56:28,724
Hey. You did enough yesterday.

792
00:56:28,724 --> 00:56:30,252
No!

793
00:56:30,252 --> 00:56:32,959
I won't let you off, Sung Sae Ryeong.

794
00:56:32,959 --> 00:56:35,453
Are you throwing all that?

795
00:56:35,453 --> 00:56:37,439
What if a teacher catches you?

796
00:56:37,439 --> 00:56:40,084
What, are you scared?

797
00:56:40,776 --> 00:56:42,679
Then you guys don't do it.

798
00:56:42,679 --> 00:56:45,057
You're damn cowards.

799
00:56:45,057 --> 00:56:46,143
What?

800
00:56:47,893 --> 00:56:49,186
- Hey.
- Hey.

801
00:56:59,348 --> 00:57:01,839
Hey. What's she trying to do now?

802
00:57:01,839 --> 00:57:04,250
- No idea.
- What's with her?

803
00:57:05,797 --> 00:57:07,451
It's okay. It's okay.

804
00:57:19,374 --> 00:57:21,047
What are you doing?

805
00:57:22,648 --> 00:57:23,792
What's that?

806
00:57:23,792 --> 00:57:24,947
Hey, what are you doing?

807
00:57:24,947 --> 00:57:25,984
- What?
- What?

808
00:57:25,984 --> 00:57:27,191
What are you doing?

809
00:57:27,191 --> 00:57:28,931
Jin Mi, stop it.

810
00:57:34,542 --> 00:57:36,331
- Who is that?
- Who is that?

811
00:57:36,331 --> 00:57:38,265
- Isn't that Jin Mi?
- What?

812
00:57:42,334 --> 00:57:44,872
Damn. That's pure insanity.

813
00:58:01,648 --> 00:58:02,941
How do you like it?

814
00:58:02,941 --> 00:58:05,297
This is the world you gave me.

815
00:58:12,280 --> 00:58:14,995
Stop it.

816
00:58:45,692 --> 00:58:46,827
Hey, what?

817
00:58:46,827 --> 00:58:48,099
Hey, it's Cho Yu Gyeom!

818
00:58:48,099 --> 00:58:49,279
Hey, it's Cho Yu Gyeom.

819
00:58:49,279 --> 00:58:51,520
Didn't they break up?

820
00:58:51,520 --> 00:58:53,292
He'll stop them, right?

821
00:58:58,015 --> 00:58:59,054
What are you doing?

822
00:58:59,054 --> 00:59:00,971
- Just dodge it!
- Why dodge?

823
00:59:00,971 --> 00:59:02,730
After acting scary,

824
00:59:03,506 --> 00:59:05,147
now acting pitiful?

825
00:59:06,233 --> 00:59:08,510
Do you even pity me?

826
00:59:19,893 --> 00:59:21,596
Hey! Kim Jin Mi!

827
00:59:21,596 --> 00:59:23,187
You little brat!

828
00:59:24,048 --> 00:59:25,080
What are you doing?

829
00:59:25,080 --> 00:59:26,603
Let go! Let go!

830
00:59:27,689 --> 00:59:29,002
Let go!

831
00:59:30,823 --> 00:59:32,694
Jin Mi.

832
00:59:32,694 --> 00:59:34,638
- Let me go!
- Please.

833
00:59:34,638 --> 00:59:36,337
Please!

834
00:59:36,337 --> 00:59:39,997
Cho Yu Gyeom, if you have nothing,
this is how you get cleaned out.

835
00:59:39,997 --> 00:59:41,073
You know?

836
00:59:41,753 --> 00:59:43,602
Do you know what comes next?

837
00:59:45,639 --> 00:59:47,237
Me dying.

838
00:59:47,986 --> 00:59:50,553
Because that's what they want.

839
00:59:50,553 --> 00:59:52,725
And that's the gift you gave me--

840
00:59:52,725 --> 00:59:53,827
Then,

841
01:00:00,392 --> 01:00:01,959
if I do this...

842
01:00:02,853 --> 01:00:04,608
- What?
- What?

843
01:00:07,500 --> 01:00:09,233
no one can touch you?

844
01:00:09,233 --> 01:00:11,698
- What are you doing?
- Tell me.

845
01:00:13,944 --> 01:00:15,879
Will this keep you alive?

846
01:00:20,037 --> 01:00:22,468
What I saw then was...

847
01:00:23,599 --> 01:00:24,978
as if...

848
01:00:25,886 --> 01:00:30,033
by fate... the two of you, so alike.

849
01:00:30,033 --> 01:00:33,500
Are they getting back together? Crazy.

850
01:00:33,500 --> 01:00:35,346
This is such a soap opera.

851
01:00:35,346 --> 01:00:37,578
It's totally over the top.

852
01:00:38,847 --> 01:00:40,596
If I, too,

853
01:00:40,596 --> 01:00:46,288
had known from the start
that it would end up this way.

854
01:00:51,318 --> 01:00:53,407
I knew we'd end up like this.

855
01:00:54,420 --> 01:00:56,020
What?

856
01:00:56,020 --> 01:01:00,109
In the end, you're the one who saves me.

857
01:01:18,386 --> 01:01:19,741
Yu Gyeom.

858
01:01:21,627 --> 01:01:25,767
Our summer vacation is coming to an end.
